<p class="sig-footnote source-note"><span class="sig-sup">*</span> = bank's non-customer recall for this CEP is at least 8 percentage points above the average across the other five banks (a proxy for two-proportion z-test significance at α=0.10 in this design).</p>

<div class="opp-callout">
<p><strong>Simplii's CEP signature.</strong> Simplii has 100% recall among its own customers for everyday spending and bill payments and 35% among non-customers, the largest buyer-to-non-buyer gap in the dataset. Simplii also has a smaller but real lift on digital banking (74% of own customers, 57% of non-customers). Simplii has zero mentions on mortgage shopping, retirement and investing, financial advice for life events, and small-business banking, from anyone, including its own customers. Interpretation: Simplii's two-CEP mental footprint is a rational fit with its product scope; the everyday-spending non-customer gap is the highest-ROI lever for brand-building investment.</p>
