<h3>3e. Simplii vs Tangerine (qualitative)</h3>
<p>Tangerine is not a primary-bank cohort in the sample and not in the mental-availability battery, so quantitative comparison is not available. Where Simplii wins vs Tangerine: (a) the CIBC ATM moat (58% of Simplii customers name the shared ATM network as a reason they chose Simplii; Tangerine has no equivalent of comparable scale), (b) parent-credibility cushion that reduces perceived switching anxiety for CIBC-origin defectors, and (c) specific product gaps at Tangerine (US$ checking availability, small-business). Where Tangerine may win: stronger brand marketing and longer tenure as a standalone digital-bank brand.</p>
<p>Among the 85 participants who considered Simplii during their switch evaluation and chose not to pick it, the rejection reasons are the same ones any digital challenger would face: no physical branch access 87%, having heard a negative story secondhand 65%, concerns about a lateral move 61%, app-quality concerns 52%. Tangerine faces the same structural resistance.</p>

