<h3>7b. Dissatisfaction signals</h3>
<p>See Section 5a for the full frustration chart. The three structural frustrations (limited product breadth, no branch, unwanted fragmentation) are not retention risks in themselves; 75 to 82% of the Simplii customers who cite them are still satisfied with the bank overall. The fixable dissatisfiers are savings rate (35% cite as a current frustration) and phone waits (37%).</p>

<h3>7c. Contingent stayer segmentation</h3>
<p>Three tiers derived from the forward-looking propensity question, the count of current frustrations a participant cited, and whether they hold products elsewhere. Definitions are strict; "stable loyalist" requires both high satisfaction AND no more than one current frustration.</p>

